# ============================================================================
#  gpgpu-sim-h3-backend.patch -- add the H3 memory backend to GPGPU-Sim
# ============================================================================
#  WHAT THIS DOES
#      Adds a third memory backend alongside the two GPGPU-Sim already has.
#      Selection follows the EXACT pattern of the existing
#      -gpgpu_simple_dram_model option (registered at gpu-sim.cc:243,
#      dispatched at gpu-sim.cc:2295), so both existing paths are untouched
#      and default behaviour is bit-identical to upstream.
#
#          -gpgpu_memory_backend 0   default dram_t          (unchanged)
#          -gpgpu_memory_backend 1   simple fixed-latency    (unchanged)
#          -gpgpu_memory_backend 2   H3 (HBM + HBF + LHB)    (new)
#
#  WHY A PATCH RATHER THAN EDITING THE TREE
#      gpu-simulator/gpgpu-sim/ is cloned from upstream by
#      setup_environment.sh and is not tracked by this repository. Keeping the
#      change as a patch means it is version-controlled here, reviewable as a
#      diff, and `git status` in the upstream tree stays clean.
#
#  APPLY / REVERT
#      ./scripts/apply_gpgpu_sim_patch.sh
#      ./scripts/apply_gpgpu_sim_patch.sh --revert
#      ./scripts/apply_gpgpu_sim_patch.sh --check     (dry run)
#
#  GENERATED, NOT HAND-WRITTEN
#      Produced with `diff -u` from real edited sources, so the hunk offsets
#      are correct by construction. Verified to apply cleanly against
#      gpgpu-sim_distribution @ dev.
# ============================================================================
